-- title:
--   Measurability of the first unsatisfiability time of a clause stream
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n$ and $k$, and write $[n]=\{0,1,\dots,n-1\}$ for the set of Boolean variables. An *assignment* is a map $a:[n]\to\{\mathrm T,\mathrm F\}$. A *clause of width $k$* is a pair $c=(V,\beta)$ of a set $V\subseteq[n]$ with $|V|=k$ and a sign map $\beta:V\to\{\mathrm T,\mathrm F\}$; the assignment $a$ *satisfies* $c$ if $a(v)=\beta(v)$ for at least one $v\in V$. Let $\mathcal C_{n,k}$ be the finite set of all such clauses; it has $\binom nk2^k$ elements.
--
--   A *stream* is an infinite sequence $\omega=(\omega_0,\omega_1,\omega_2,\dots)$ of clauses from $\mathcal C_{n,k}$. Write $\mathrm{SAT}_m(\omega)$ if some single assignment satisfies all of $\omega_0,\dots,\omega_{m-1}$ (for $m=0$ this always holds). The *first failure time* of $\omega$ is $\tau(\omega)=\min\{m\in\mathbb N:\ \mathrm{SAT}_m(\omega)\text{ fails}\}\in\mathbb N\cup\{\infty\}$, with $\tau(\omega)=\infty$ if every prefix is satisfiable.
--
--   Equip $\mathcal C_{n,k}$ with the discrete $\sigma$-algebra, the space $\mathcal C_{n,k}^{\mathbb N}$ of streams with the product $\sigma$-algebra (generated by the coordinate maps $\omega\mapsto\omega_i$), and $\mathbb N\cup\{\infty\}$ with the discrete $\sigma$-algebra.
--
--   **Theorem.** For all $n,k\in\mathbb N$ the first failure time
--   $$
--   \tau:\ \mathcal C_{n,k}^{\mathbb N}\to\mathbb N\cup\{\infty\}
--   $$
--   is measurable. Equivalently, $\{\omega:\ \tau(\omega)\in A\}$ is a measurable set of streams for every $A\subseteq\mathbb N\cup\{\infty\}$.
--
--   Consequently $\tau$ is a random variable under any probability measure on streams, in particular under the law of independent uniformly random clauses. The same then holds for every function of $\tau$, such as the real-valued first failure time and its truncation at a cap, whose variances are the subject of the random $k$-SAT variance estimates.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is `Measurable (firstFailure : Stream n k → ℕ∞)`. Here `Stream n k` is `ℕ → Clause n k` with the product measurable space, the clause type carries the discrete measurable space `⊤`, and Mathlib's measurable space on `ℕ∞` is also `⊤`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Probability/SATVariance/FirstFailure.lean#L93-L110

